; Tutorial_2_Install_and_Tune_In.inix -- the installer, DbDo opening on RadioTrail, and a station found by name and playing.

[about]
Title=2 - Install and Tune In
Intro=DbDo installed with what it works best with, opened from anywhere, and on its first run a station from RadioTrail found by name and playing.
Setup=The DbDo setup program is downloaded.
Homework=Find and play a station you already know, by its name.

[step]

Say=One want: DbDo on this computer, and a station playing, in one sitting.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=I open the downloaded setup program and allow it to make changes.
Key=Enter
Hear=Setup - DbDo dialog
Hear=Welcome to the DbDo Setup Wizard
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The ordinary installer: Enter takes Next, and the defaults are right.
Key=Enter
Hear=Select Destination Location
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The last page offers what DbDo works best with, each as a box whose first word is your computer's state read for you: Install, Update or Reinstall.
Key=Tab
Hear=Install mpv, plays a station for Play Stream, checked, 1 of 4
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Scripts for the screen reader you use; the mpv player, which plays a station; and, for the AI commands, Ollama and a model, downloaded once. Install and Update are ticked; Reinstall is not, since what is current needs nothing.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: clearing a box you need. Space clears it; Space again ticks it back.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked

[step]

Say=Space.
Key=Space
Hear=checked

[step]

Say=Enter installs what is ticked, and then the key that opens DbDo from anywhere.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=The first time, DbDo opens RadioTrail: internet radio stations, one to a row. The ten streams of the American Council of the Blind and the NFB Radio Network come first, then every other station by name. Shift plus Z says so.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=stations, 55280 records, no filter, sorted by source, name
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The first station is already one of them. Insert plus Up Arrow says the line again.
Key=Insert+Up Arrow
Hear=ACB Media 1, The United States Of America, ACB Media, blindness, Row 1 of 55280
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus I, Inspect Record, shows the whole record, one field to a line.
Key=Control+I
Hear=Inspect Record dialog
Hear=name: ACB Media 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Its genre, country, language, and the address it streams from. Escape. Now the reason RadioTrail opens first: Alt plus Shift plus P, Play Stream, plays the station in the Homer Player.
Key=Alt+Shift+P
Hear=Homer Player, ACB Media 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the player. A station I already know is quickest found by its name. Control plus J, Jump to Record, asks which column and what to look for.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump to Record dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I leave the column as name, type K E X P, and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=KEXP, The United States Of America, various, Row 19193 of 55280
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus J jumps backward to the match before, as Shift reverses everywhere in DbDo. Another database opens with Control plus O, and a template with Alt plus Shift plus D, D for Database.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Two help keys belong to this walk. Alt plus F1, About, says which DbDo is installed.
Key=Alt+F1
Hear=About DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, and F11 asks GitHub whether a newer version is out. If one is, Enter installs it.
Key=F11
Hear=Checking for a newer version
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Installed, open and playing. If something was left out, run the setup again and tick its box; what is already current costs nothing.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The key that opens DbDo.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus D

[step]

Say=Find a record by one column.
Key=
Hear=Control plus J

[step]

Say=Play the station.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus P
